\title{The type of Spaces is a Segal}
\tag{Changelog}
\author{samueltoth}
\contributor{fredrikbakke}
\date{2026-08-30}
\meta{source}{[PR\startverb#\stopverb218](https://github.com/samtoth/agda-synthetic-categories/pull/218)}
\meta{source}{[PR\startverb#\stopverb220](https://github.com/samtoth/agda-synthetic-categories/pull/220)}
\meta{source}{[PR\startverb#\stopverb225](https://github.com/samtoth/agda-synthetic-categories/pull/225)}
\import{stt-macros}


\p{This changelog details the work I have done recently on
cleaning up and extending the formalisation of the category of
Spaces.}

\ul{
  \li{Firstly cleans up a hole in the original proof, namely that #{X \to Y} is covariant for
  contravariant families #{X} and covariant families #{Y}.}
  \li{A nice lemma about fibrewise equivalences of covariant families using all cubes separate.}
  \li{We can liberate directed univalence from the existence of a classifying object with cohesive type theory}
  \li{This made the interface glueing reusable – can define glueing of a 2-simlex in terms of normal glueing.
      Get nice properties for free.}
  \li{We also get that in type theory with an interval, the type of left fibrations over the #{\Gamma \times \II}
      is a retract of the type of maps of left fibrations over #{\Gamma}.}
  \li{Nice little proof of Segalness as a result}
  \li{Weakening cubes separate}
  \li{Horn glueing relies on Segal-ness of #{Delta^2}, a not yet formalised consequence of cubes separate}
  \li{Still rely on the tiny type former preserving pullbacks}
}


